        "tekst": "**Four terms students mix up**\n\n**Prejudice** is an attitude about a category. **A stereotype** is the exaggerated image built from prejudices and applied to every member. **Racism** is a specific prejudice: belief in innate racial superiority or inferiority. **Discrimination** (section 4) is **behaviour**, not attitude. A classic exam trap: \"a manager believes Group X is lazy but hires them anyway because of the law\" shows prejudice **without** discrimination (Merton's timid bigot)."
